    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nGiven a configuration like:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal tsSpec = require('mini.ai').gen_spec.treesitter\r\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\r\n  custom_textobjects = {\r\n    c = tsSpec({\r\n      a = '@class.outer',\r\n      i = '@class.inner',\r\n    }, {})\r\n  }\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt would be nice to be able to put something like `desc` to use in conjunction with which-key or legendary or whatever to describe the keymap.",
