    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is an interesting idea. It has at least one, but pretty significant obstacle: 'mini.ai' only defines `a` and `i` mappings along with their `next`/`last` variants. They implement their custom waiting for character input, which allows users to take their time when deciding what to press. This is a part of 'which-key' type of functionality.\r\n\r\nI *think* it should be possible to add custom description to already existing mappings inside 'folke/which-key.nvim'.",
