        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I _think_ it should be possible to add custom description to already existing mappings inside 'folke/which-key.nvim'.\r\n\r\nWell, now I *think* that it is nearly impossible to cleanly use 'mini.ai' textobjects with something like 'folke/which-key.nvim' and 'mrjones2014/legendary.nvim' because it uses blocking `getcharstr()` to get textobject id from user. Reasoning for this approach is indeed as from previous post: to allow user to think as long as they need before entering textobject id.",
