            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Thanks for following up. I'm a bit unclear on where the use-case for mini.ai ends and treesitter-textobjects begins. Would be nice to find a solution that \"just works\".\r\n\r\nThey both can implement additional textobjects. [Here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/96e648cae35dfd361c9077bf79306dd05d23db2f/doc/mini-align.txt#L816) is a more in-depth comparison.\r\n\r\nYou can use queries from 'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects' to define tree-sitter-aware textobjects with 'mini.ai'. This is supposed to be done by adding specifications for custom textobjects in `config.custom_textobjects`. There is a [`MiniAi.gen_spec.treesitter()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/96e648cae35dfd361c9077bf79306dd05d23db2f/doc/mini-ai.txt#L645) helper which generates specifications based on captures from 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects'. It has example of how to use it.",
            "created_at": "2023-01-12T18:09:47Z",
